{"skill":{"slug":"file-search","displayName":"File Search"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770135651974,"changelog":"Initial publish","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"CLAUDE.md","size":303,"sha256":"aa170881be075885cbe1e173bd234fb526cd3f4606331d254fd6eca690c6ff6f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1208,"sha256":"e565d8d1a08a9d3ec7426d704d58dc15d3fc9384ec3e882e4f77e627825c018e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1485,"sha256":"26a8b916f7544a73be206b92ba0c8091c8a26d07ff07ea051b5402d949c452ae","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031043982,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"183fa51c439ad3e928361bc9ba664c7a8dbe2ef3a61ca137e8fd56b2071f9094","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/183fa51c439ad3e928361bc9ba664c7a8dbe2ef3a61ca137e8fd56b2071f9094","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: file-search\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for 'file-search' is benign. It clearly defines its purpose as fast file-name and content search using standard tools `fd` and `rg`. The `SKILL.md` provides legitimate installation instructions via `dnf` for standard packages (`fd-find`, `ripgrep`) and examples of using these tools for local file system searches. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent. The `CLAUDE.md` file contains only benign activity logs.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161118879},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":7,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789031043982},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward file-search helper; the only elevated action is a disclosed package-manager install for common search tools.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The tools can read file names and matching file contents under whatever paths the user asks the agent to search, which is inherent to the stated file-search purpose.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The install section uses sudo dnf install fd-find ripgrep, which is elevated but clearly disclosed and consistent with installing the declared fd and rg dependencies.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are narrow examples for finding files and searching contents; no hidden agent directives, credential access, remote payloads, or automatic execution behavior were found.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installing OS packages persists beyond the skill run, but there are no services, hooks, scheduled tasks, backdoors, or privilege-retaining mechanisms in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill purpose is fast file-name and content search, and the runtime guidance only demonstrates fd and rg commands for user-specified paths and patterns.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable adding fd-find and ripgrep through your system package manager. Before running the sudo command, confirm the packages and distro match your environment; once installed, searches should be limited to directories you intend the agent to inspect.","findings":"[PE2] expected: The sudo finding is limited to a documented dnf package-install command for fd-find and ripgrep; it is not used for runtime search, privilege retention, or unrelated system modification.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031043982}}}}}